00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:08.039
TAD EINSTEIN: So
today is going to be

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:09.240
a very interesting session.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.090
So GitLab, as you may
or may not be aware,

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.640
migrated from Azure into GCP.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.340
And the goal of this session
was a complete, honest session

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.370
of why they did it,
thoughts behind it,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.277
the pros, the cons, and really
help so that you can understand

00:00:23.277 --> 00:00:25.860
what a real-world company does
who has a lot of customers when

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.400
they're looking to do a
migration of this sort

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.270
and a lot of the considerations
that go into play.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.910
So first some
quick housekeeping.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.370
We have something
called the Dory.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.870
So the Dory is
what's going to allow

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.780
