answers throughout the event.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.130
So feel free to
log into your app.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.848
You'll see right there
where it says Dory Q&amp;A.

00:00:44.848 --> 00:00:46.140
And then you can ask questions.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.765
At the end, we'll
answer the questions.

00:00:47.765 --> 00:00:49.590
As well as you can
come up to the mic so

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.580
we can dive a bit deeper.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.950
So with that being
said, let's get started.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.010
So first thing I'm just
quickly going to touch on

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.340
is Google Cloud's migration
path and our methodology.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.160
So whenever you're doing
a migration, whether it's

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.860
on prem to on prem, on prem
to cloud, cloud to cloud,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.780
or whatever the future
is going to bring,

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.050
you need to have a very
methodological approach-- so

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.330
the idea of assessing
what's in your environment.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.130
Anyone who's ever done
this and tried just

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.580
moving something to the cloud
often breaks 20 other systems.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.010
So it's very important
understanding technically

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.870
what's there, the cost when
you're going to move it,

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:24.995
but also how are all the
things are interconnected,

00:01:24.995 --> 00:01:27.078
because you want to move
things in the right order

00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:28.320
and the right move groups.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.340
So you assess.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.750
You understand what's there.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.145
The next step is setting
up your landing zone.

00:01:33.145 --> 00:01:34.770
So what environment
is it going to look

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.690
like when you come
to Google Cloud

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.335
so that you can begin migrating?

00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:39.960
So you set up things
like your Identity

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.310
and Access Management,
security, various policies,

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.710
connectivity, maybe
back to a data center

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.270
and additional cloud.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.848
Once that's all set
up, then you can

00:01:49.848 --> 00:01:52.140
do the fun part, which is
actually migrating and moving

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.245
to the cloud.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.870
When you're in the
cloud, the next step

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.180
is optimizing, because usually
there's a reason people

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.010
move to the cloud.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.500
And there are a lot of benefits
around operationalizing

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.430
and taking it to the next level.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.820
So with that being said, I'm
going to bring Brandon up

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.037
onstage, and he'll talk a bit
about how GitLab got there.

