00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.580
My job here is to give you
a context of what GitLab

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.530
is for a very simple reason.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.650
GitLab.com or
GitLab as a company,

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.400
we're a single DevOps tool.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.760
So we cover everything
from how you go down,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.915
how software developers
write software.

00:02:49.915 --> 00:02:51.540
This is what they
live in all day long.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.150
They go from the planning
ideas, writing their software,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.630
testing it for quality, ensuring
that it has great security,

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.340
packaging up and deploying
it in to production,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.370
and even eventually
monitoring it.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.860
So this is what GitLab does.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.900
What we're talking about
today is GitLab.com.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.570
So there's two primary ways
